    {
      "key": "team.reading.a2.weekend-trip",
      "kind": "ReadingPassage",
      "values": {
        "Title": "A Weekend Trip",
        "Content": "Last Saturday my family took a bus to the beach. The weather was warm and sunny, so we did not need jackets. We walked on the soft sand and collected small shells near the water. My little brother built a small castle with a stick and laughed when the waves touched it.\n\nIn the afternoon we ate fresh fish at a small restaurant by the road. Then we swam in the sea for almost an hour. My father took many photos of the blue water. Children nearby played football, and music came from a radio on the sand.\n\nOn the way home I was tired, but I felt excited about the trip. I want to go again next month if the weather is good and we have free time. My mother already put the shells in a small box on the shelf.",
        "Level": "A2",
        "Topic": "Travel",
        "ImageUrl": "asset:48d9b2c1f868d709512f910a628a30d012de43e33dd73de18e26267e19d14eeb.jpg",
